// CE4 (complaint-roadmap): a batch of compiler error-message tests —
// each function triggers a distinct error; the _fail suffix means the
// compiler must reject it. These cover the most common type errors a
// newcomer hits. Run with `fid test` (each fn test_* runs separately).
//
// This file has no expected output — it tests that `fid check` rejects
// the _fail variants with useful messages. See the companion
// test_error_msgs_ok.fd for the passing versions.

fn main() -> i64 {
    println("error message tests: see test_error_msgs_*_fail.fd");
    return 0;
}
